+//  FRAQTL view-allocation-skip helper.
+// When fraqtl marker storage is active, layers[ikv].k / .v are backed by
+// tiny real storage with full-size nbytes claims, per /5.7. The view tensors
+// built by get_k/get_v inherit `view_src = k/v` but are created with
+// data=NULL and buffer=NULL. ggml's gallocr then reserves space for each
+// view based on its claimed nbytes (128 MiB per layer × NQ × n_streams),
+// summing to ~3.6 GiB of fake compute-buffer reservation that explodes the
+// destructor warning ("compute buffer size of 4544 MiB, does not match
+// expectation of 1254 MiB").
+// Fix: explicitly propagate the marker parent's data + buffer to the view
+// at graph-build time. gallocr's "is this tensor external?" check (data ||
+// buffer) then passes and no fresh reservation is made. The view's claimed
+// nbytes (128 MiB) is metadata only — actual K/V reads at execute time are
+// intercepted by fraqtl's K dispatcher (fattn.cu fraqtl_k=true template)
+// and V's apply_U_T_to_O path. view->data being a 128-byte marker is never
+// dereferenced.
